     "explainHtml": "<span class=\"math-inline\"><math dir=\"ltr\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\log n</annotation></semantics></math></span> אינו <span class=\"math-inline\"><math dir=\"ltr\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Θ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Theta(1)</annotation></semantics></math></span> (מקרה 2) כי הוא גדל, ואינו <span class=\"math-inline\"><math dir=\"ltr\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\Omega(n^{\\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math></span> (מקרה 3) כי <span class=\"math-inline\"><math dir=\"ltr\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\log n/n^{\\epsilon}\\to 0</annotation></semantics></math></span> לכל <span class=\"math-inline\"><math dir=\"ltr\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math></span> (נבדק סימבולית). מקרה 1 דורש ש-<span class=\"math-inline\"><math dir=\"ltr\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">f</annotation></semantics></math></span> יהיה קטן מ-<span class=\"math-inline\"><math dir=\"ltr\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">n^2</annotation></semantics></math></span>, וכאן הוא גדול ממנו."
